[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit, 4.Ng5"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,hanging-piece"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5 4. Ng5"]
[Themes "queen-diagonal,f7-moved"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "4.Ng5"]
[Start "rousseau-gambit 3...f5"]

4. Ng5 $2 { Looks like the usual attack on f7, but the f-pawn has already moved and nothing guards the knight. } 4... Qxg5 { The queen sees all the way to g5 along the diagonal now that the f7 pawn has left, and takes the knight for nothing. } 5. O-O f4 { Keeps the extra knight and gains space; White has no attack for a whole piece. } 6. Nc3 Nf6 *
